(606272, 62121, 16775, '<td valign="top">bland.  there is a uniformity of texture and color across the whole photo (with the obvious exception of her face).  it loks like so many photos you see in family albums.  perhaps there''s something to be said for that - the "conflict"  that exists in every "typical family"<br/> <br/>not sure if i buy it though...</td>', 'bland.  there is a uniformity of texture and color across the whole photo (with the obvious exception of her face).  it loks like so many photos you see in family albums.  perhaps there''s something to be said for that - the "conflict"  that exists in every "typical family" not sure if i buy it though...', '2004-03-02 23:21:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(606274, 61319, 17203, '<td valign="top">Good choice for this challenge. Beautiful composition and lighting. The only things I can pick on are that the snow is obviously blown out and the cannon''s shadow might have been more interesting at a later time of day (plus, you would have picked up shadows in the snow). Still, this is one of my top three picks. Nicely done!</td>', 'Good choice for this challenge. Beautiful composition and lighting. The only things I can pick on are that the snow is obviously blown out and the cannon''s shadow might have been more interesting at a later time of day (plus, you would have picked up shadows in the snow). Still, this is one of my top three picks. Nicely done!', '2004-03-02 23:22:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(606276, 61974, 16775, '<td valign="top">i would like to see this one framed in MUCH closer.  i want to see the detail of the fish in his mouth.  if you could get it so that the entire photo would be composed of his eye at the extreme upper left edge and the tip of his beak at the lower right - i think that would make it a bit more dramatic.</td>', 'i would like to see this one framed in MUCH closer.  i want to see the detail of the fish in his mouth.  if you could get it so that the entire photo would be composed of his eye at the extreme upper left edge and the tip of his beak at the lower right - i think that would make it a bit more dramatic.', '2004-03-02 23:24:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(606278, 62066, 16775, '<td valign="top">congrats on the statement (whoever raised them in this order) but it seems almost blasphemous.  i don''t care for the grain in the sky either.</td>', 'congrats on the statement (whoever raised them in this order) but it seems almost blasphemous.  i don''t care for the grain in the sky either.', '2004-03-02 23:26:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(606279, 61582, 17203, '<td valign="top">Clearly one of the top shots this week. Too bad the lioness wasn''t more confrontational (or at least facing him), but you don''t have much control over that.  ;-)</td>', 'Clearly one of the top shots this week. Too bad the lioness wasn''t more confrontational (or at least facing him), but you don''t have much control over that.  ;-)', '2004-03-02 23:26:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(606282, 61939, 16775, '<td valign="top">i don''t have much of a problem with the composition given the subject. (sorry :)<br/> <br/>it seems way too forced or staged.  why the guitar?  i don''t buy it.</td>', 'i don''t have much of a problem with the composition given the subject. (sorry :) it seems way too forced or staged.  why the guitar?  i don''t buy it.', '2004-03-02 23:27:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(606289, 61582, 16775, '<td valign="top">any wild life is almost guaranteed to be photogenic... ALMOST<br/> <br/>i don''t mind this one so much.  i do wish the lioness''s hind legs weren''t cropped.  try to be aware of what is happening at the EDGES of your shots.   the subject is the easy part to get - make sure things bleed off of it in a nice controlled manner. i usually use textures or lines at the edges of my shots (notice how well the rest of the photo works at the edge...the green bamboo shoots, the concrete, the straw, but then the lions leg...<br/> <br/>oh well  not bad :)</td>', 'any wild life is almost guaranteed to be photogenic... ALMOST i don''t mind this one so much.  i do wish the lioness''s hind legs weren''t cropped.  try to be aware of what is happening at the EDGES of your shots.   the subject is the easy part to get - make sure things bleed off of it in a nice controlled manner. i usually use textures or lines at the edges of my shots (notice how well the rest of the photo works at the edge...the green bamboo shoots, the concrete, the straw, but then the lions leg... oh well  not bad :)', '2004-03-02 23:32:28.000000', NULL, 1),
