(607145, 61924, 11295, '<td valign="top">Hey! Much thanks for all the comments. This one smashes my record for comments received on a photo. Must admit, I was quite pleased.<br/> <br/>To answer some questions:<br/> <br/>The prey was a rabbit. I took about 30 shots of this scene, and some show unmistakable rabbit-like qualities in that mess (the hawk was quite set on his dinner... he was there for a good 15 minutes)<br/> <br/>I did not bait the predator. Although I don''t know if he killed it himself, he was already eating when I arrived. This hawk has apparently been loitering about the office complex for some time now. Never saw him this close before though.<br/> <br/>The shot is indeed "in the wild" although it''s not really ''wild'' when you consider it''s on a fairly well travelled street. To get the shot, I used my Sigma 70-300mm AF lens. I was about 25 metres from the bird at the time I took the shot. Amazingly, it was hand held - I didn''t have my tripod with me. Seems I have a steadier grasp than I thought. :)<br/> <br/>Thanks again, all!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-03 09:37:08.</i></td>', 'Hey! Much thanks for all the comments. This one smashes my record for comments received on a photo. Must admit, I was quite pleased. To answer some questions: The prey was a rabbit. I took about 30 shots of this scene, and some show unmistakable rabbit-like qualities in that mess (the hawk was quite set on his dinner... he was there for a good 15 minutes) I did not bait the predator. Although I don''t know if he killed it himself, he was already eating when I arrived. This hawk has apparently been loitering about the office complex for some time now. Never saw him this close before though. The shot is indeed "in the wild" although it''s not really ''wild'' when you consider it''s on a fairly well travelled street. To get the shot, I used my Sigma 70-300mm AF lens. I was about 25 metres from the bird at the time I took the shot. Amazingly, it was hand held - I didn''t have my tripod with me. Seems I have a steadier grasp than I thought. :) Thanks again, all!', '2004-03-03 09:34:45.000000', '2004-03-03 09:37:08.000000', 0),
(607152, 61509, 17334, '<td valign="top">Hi everybody,<br/> <br/>Thanks for your comments. It was my first participation to the challenge. I will learn.<br/> <br/>Bye<br/> <br/>Bernard <br/></td>', 'Hi everybody, Thanks for your comments. It was my first participation to the challenge. I will learn. Bye Bernard ', '2004-03-03 09:38:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(607171, 62120, 10686, '<td valign="top">Jacko!! You da man!!! Glad I could help you out with my "1" you deserved a lower score, but "1" is as low as the scale goes. Congrats on the brown ribbon. This is going in my faves, right next to the bunny shot.</td>', 'Jacko!! You da man!!! Glad I could help you out with my "1" you deserved a lower score, but "1" is as low as the scale goes. Congrats on the brown ribbon. This is going in my faves, right next to the bunny shot.', '2004-03-03 09:50:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(607187, 61757, 16648, '<td valign="top">The ''mysterious'' white bar was some kind of Photoshop ''gift''. I have no idea how it got there or why i didn''t see it.  The lighting was not as good as i had hoped for, but the best i was ablt to achieve. I am still learning! The spot light was sipposed to be equallyon the two pawns, but black is a tough color to light, especially so next to white. Thanks to all those that commented.</td>', 'The ''mysterious'' white bar was some kind of Photoshop ''gift''. I have no idea how it got there or why i didn''t see it.  The lighting was not as good as i had hoped for, but the best i was ablt to achieve. I am still learning! The spot light was sipposed to be equallyon the two pawns, but black is a tough color to light, especially so next to white. Thanks to all those that commented.', '2004-03-03 09:59:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(607220, 61482, 6624, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get to vote in this challenge but if I had this would have been my top pick.  Congratulations</td>', 'I didn''t get to vote in this challenge but if I had this would have been my top pick.  Congratulations', '2004-03-03 10:18:36.000000', NULL, 0),
