(611227, 61547, 17525, '<td valign="top">Thankyou to all who voted and commented. Certainly a sobering experience, but one may confidently infer that in its majority, this is not an audience worth ''pleasing''. That said I remain excited and inspired to participate in coming challenges, producing challenging entries that may recieve some constructive criticism and commentary. Thanks DPCHALLENGE!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-05 20:22:30.</i></td>', 'Thankyou to all who voted and commented. Certainly a sobering experience, but one may confidently infer that in its majority, this is not an audience worth ''pleasing''. That said I remain excited and inspired to participate in coming challenges, producing challenging entries that may recieve some constructive criticism and commentary. Thanks DPCHALLENGE!', '2004-03-05 19:44:09.000000', '2004-03-05 20:22:30.000000', 0),
(611333, 62116, 7969, '<td valign="top">HI greetings from the CC, well my initial thought when i saw this shot I thought would of been good if the top of fence had been cropped out, focusing the eye on the tree and snow, had you shot in aperature priority you could of added some DOF to blur the fence which again distract the viewer from the true subjects at hand.  I think that it is also the snow and tree truck is where the points of  interest are, focusing on these two elements would be my advice : ).  Also keeping strictly on challenge helps shots to score higher with most dpcers''.<br/>keep shooting</td>', 'HI greetings from the CC, well my initial thought when i saw this shot I thought would of been good if the top of fence had been cropped out, focusing the eye on the tree and snow, had you shot in aperature priority you could of added some DOF to blur the fence which again distract the viewer from the true subjects at hand.  I think that it is also the snow and tree truck is where the points of  interest are, focusing on these two elements would be my advice : ).  Also keeping strictly on challenge helps shots to score higher with most dpcers''.keep shooting', '2004-03-05 21:22:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(611568, 61929, 16075, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get a chance to vote in this challenge, but if I had, I would have given you an "F"...only 1 point.  It really ticks me off when people such as yourself feel you have to enter a photo that has nothing to do with the challenge, just because it is an excellent photo.  Bye the way, in another appropriate challenge I''m sure I would have given this a 10.  I see you have many ribbons and I am sure they were well deserved, but I think that has gone to your head and you are acting like a pompous ass!</td>', 'I didn''t get a chance to vote in this challenge, but if I had, I would have given you an "F"...only 1 point.  It really ticks me off when people such as yourself feel you have to enter a photo that has nothing to do with the challenge, just because it is an excellent photo.  Bye the way, in another appropriate challenge I''m sure I would have given this a 10.  I see you have many ribbons and I am sure they were well deserved, but I think that has gone to your head and you are acting like a pompous ass!', '2004-03-06 02:20:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(611610, 61229, 16075, '<td valign="top">By entering something that doesn''t fit the challenge you are assuring yourself a failing score.  I didn''t get time to cast a vote in this challenge, but if I had you would have received another 1 (along with the other 31 1''s you received.)  Too bad because this is a beautiful picture well worth some very high points IN THE RIGHT CHALLENGE.</td>', 'By entering something that doesn''t fit the challenge you are assuring yourself a failing score.  I didn''t get time to cast a vote in this challenge, but if I had you would have received another 1 (along with the other 31 1''s you received.)  Too bad because this is a beautiful picture well worth some very high points IN THE RIGHT CHALLENGE.', '2004-03-06 04:14:03.000000', NULL, 0),
