(612168, 61863, 14499, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SvetlanaUK:</b></div><hr/><i> This looks like one of Mr. Blobby''s photos. Great shot. I am a little tired of the "chess" setting since there are so many of those for this challenge, but this is the best one. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Bad Guess Svetlana! :)  I wouldn''t have had a shadow cast though ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by SvetlanaUK: This looks like one of Mr. Blobby''s photos. Great shot. I am a little tired of the "chess" setting since there are so many of those for this challenge, but this is the best one.   Bad Guess Svetlana! :)  I wouldn''t have had a shadow cast though ;)', '2004-03-06 20:36:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(612173, 61879, 14499, '<td valign="top">well done, the score doesn''t reflect the quality of your image. good to see you still entering shots Jarad.</td>', 'well done, the score doesn''t reflect the quality of your image. good to see you still entering shots Jarad.', '2004-03-06 20:44:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(612215, 61986, 17377, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the encouraging comment Steve.</td>', 'Thanks for the encouraging comment Steve.', '2004-03-06 21:55:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(612226, 61691, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>IMHO this shot has gone beyond the boundries of photographic integrity.  In other words it is no longer a photograph.  It is some kind of digital art and using the challenge rules as a guideline, this doesn''t truly belong on this site.<br/> <br/>Nothing personal,<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club IMHO this shot has gone beyond the boundries of photographic integrity.  In other words it is no longer a photograph.  It is some kind of digital art and using the challenge rules as a guideline, this doesn''t truly belong on this site. Nothing personal,TC', '2004-03-06 22:13:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(612256, 61653, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, well congrats on being one of the few people in the challenge who displayed conflict.  (not that i am stickler on topicality). The expression on the ''slugged'' face is fabulous, I think you did very well at capturing the feeling of being hit, the half opened eyes, stunned feel...I am suprised this shot did not do much better.  the black and white and the lighting are also very well done, clear sharp with nice tones.  I like the compostion and the fact that the hand seems to come out of no where, adding to the feeling/expression of the guy being hit.  <br/>Very good job, well done and keep shooting : )</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, well congrats on being one of the few people in the challenge who displayed conflict.  (not that i am stickler on topicality). The expression on the ''slugged'' face is fabulous, I think you did very well at capturing the feeling of being hit, the half opened eyes, stunned feel...I am suprised this shot did not do much better.  the black and white and the lighting are also very well done, clear sharp with nice tones.  I like the compostion and the fact that the hand seems to come out of no where, adding to the feeling/expression of the guy being hit.  Very good job, well done and keep shooting : )', '2004-03-06 23:00:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(612565, 62120, 10275, '<td valign="top">I''ve been sick for two weeks and haven''t been here much, but to come to this kind of entertainment is just great :-)) This just rose my spirits :-)) I can''t stop chuckling. What a crazy crowd we are... Waaaay to go Jacko!</td>', 'I''ve been sick for two weeks and haven''t been here much, but to come to this kind of entertainment is just great :-)) This just rose my spirits :-)) I can''t stop chuckling. What a crazy crowd we are... Waaaay to go Jacko!', '2004-03-07 08:24:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(613781, 61929, 656, '<td valign="top">all this unresolved sexual tension - now if you could have just photographed that!</td>', 'all this unresolved sexual tension - now if you could have just photographed that!', '2004-03-08 10:30:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(613824, 62120, 2716, '<td valign="top">Original title: angry kitty ready for a scratch your eyes (intentional abstract; if you give me a 1 you''re stupid)<br/> <br/>- Looks like it changed when I changed the title for DPCPrints.com.</td>', 'Original title: angry kitty ready for a scratch your eyes (intentional abstract; if you give me a 1 you''re stupid) - Looks like it changed when I changed the title for DPCPrints.com.', '2004-03-08 10:37:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(613861, 61582, 7969, '<td valign="top">Hi greetings from the CC, well you certainly found a conflict : ), I am glad I am not in this cage. I will start with saying this is a great capture, and often to get a good capture some things have to fall by the way side, in a perfect world the things I think that would of improved your shot a little would be,  a bit more room on  the bottom so back paws and tail not cut off. A higher aperature to get a bit of DOF would of blurred the background possibly enough so that you could fool some viewers that the shot was taken at the zoo.  Overall however very good capture with great exposure, and sharp.  I am enthralled by the lions paw size.  Good work and happy shooting!</td>', 'Hi greetings from the CC, well you certainly found a conflict : ), I am glad I am not in this cage. I will start with saying this is a great capture, and often to get a good capture some things have to fall by the way side, in a perfect world the things I think that would of improved your shot a little would be,  a bit more room on  the bottom so back paws and tail not cut off. A higher aperature to get a bit of DOF would of blurred the background possibly enough so that you could fool some viewers that the shot was taken at the zoo.  Overall however very good capture with great exposure, and sharp.  I am enthralled by the lions paw size.  Good work and happy shooting!', '2004-03-08 10:53:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(614399, 62102, 7969, '<td valign="top">Hi greetings from the CC, I find this subject while fitting the topic of limited appeal, while on dpc fitting the topic is key to a lot of participants, yet I think finding images that are engaging outside the challenge is important as well.  IMO producing shots that show emotion or have an ability to wow the viewer are the goals of our craft.  I would encourage you to find subjects that (perhaps fit the challenge) that are also engaging and have a universal vs. limited appeal.  Just my thoughts, hope it helps.  Technically, the shot is sharp, the lighting is ok but looks a bit shadowed?.  Happy shooting!</td>', 'Hi greetings from the CC, I find this subject while fitting the topic of limited appeal, while on dpc fitting the topic is key to a lot of participants, yet I think finding images that are engaging outside the challenge is important as well.  IMO producing shots that show emotion or have an ability to wow the viewer are the goals of our craft.  I would encourage you to find subjects that (perhaps fit the challenge) that are also engaging and have a universal vs. limited appeal.  Just my thoughts, hope it helps.  Technically, the shot is sharp, the lighting is ok but looks a bit shadowed?.  Happy shooting!', '2004-03-08 17:50:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(614407, 62149, 7969, '<td valign="top">Hi greetings from the CC.  IMP this image does not display too much conflict, tho I am not such a topic stickler.  I think one of the biggest challenges in photography is choosing a subject, I think it is important   IMO that the topic has some universal appeal, and a topic like ''conflict'' is emotional in nature, I think this shot is emotionally flat.  <br/>As far as strictly technical, the DOF is done well, I would like to see some more color in the shot to add some drama, perhaps with a darker bckgrnd and some softer lighting? Or food dye in the water?<br/>Being a studio type shot I would of also given a little more room on the top and bottom so subjects not so close to edges.  <br/>Hope this was not too harsh a comment, and that it is food for thought, keep shooting!</td>', 'Hi greetings from the CC.  IMP this image does not display too much conflict, tho I am not such a topic stickler.  I think one of the biggest challenges in photography is choosing a subject, I think it is important   IMO that the topic has some universal appeal, and a topic like ''conflict'' is emotional in nature, I think this shot is emotionally flat.  As far as strictly technical, the DOF is done well, I would like to see some more color in the shot to add some drama, perhaps with a darker bckgrnd and some softer lighting? Or food dye in the water?Being a studio type shot I would of also given a little more room on the top and bottom so subjects not so close to edges.  Hope this was not too harsh a comment, and that it is food for thought, keep shooting!', '2004-03-08 17:58:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(614408, 61791, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, I think what i find most lacking in your shot is some perspective, it is a bit too close up to really tell what it is.  I think it is an interesting interpretation of topic but without title not sure I would of known what it is.  Taking a few steps back may have really helped IMO.  I also think that if you use an ''ordinary'' subject i.e. car, that you need to do something to make it grab your attn. I would like to see more of the damage.  Perhaps using the mirror as a point of interest to reflect more would of been nice too.  Just some ideas hope it helps,  keep shooting.</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, I think what i find most lacking in your shot is some perspective, it is a bit too close up to really tell what it is.  I think it is an interesting interpretation of topic but without title not sure I would of known what it is.  Taking a few steps back may have really helped IMO.  I also think that if you use an ''ordinary'' subject i.e. car, that you need to do something to make it grab your attn. I would like to see more of the damage.  Perhaps using the mirror as a point of interest to reflect more would of been nice too.  Just some ideas hope it helps,  keep shooting.', '2004-03-08 18:03:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(614421, 61982, 15934, '<td valign="top">This was a classic situation of having 100 photos from the session to choose from, and I should have picked a more dynamic one.  I was in love with the composition and squelched my concern that it looked too staged.  The people (en masse) did not overlook that little wrinkle!  One thing that came out of this was that I realized that photographing people is harder and more fun than still life.  And stdavidson, I''m a real hotshot, that''s why. :)</td>', 'This was a classic situation of having 100 photos from the session to choose from, and I should have picked a more dynamic one.  I was in love with the composition and squelched my concern that it looked too staged.  The people (en masse) did not overlook that little wrinkle!  One thing that came out of this was that I realized that photographing people is harder and more fun than still life.  And stdavidson, I''m a real hotshot, that''s why. :)', '2004-03-08 18:24:34.000000', NULL, 0),
